eBoundaries":{"min":"auto","max":"auto"},"autoSelectVisualization":false,"unitsOverrides":[{"identifier":"value","unitCategory":"time","baseUnit":"millisecond","displayUnit":null,"decimals":2,"suffix":"","delimiter":false,"added":1744056596487}]},"querySettings":{"maxResultRecords":1000,"defaultScanLimitGbytes":-1,"maxResultMegaBytes":1,"defaultSamplingRatio":10,"enableSampling":false},"davis":{"enabled":false,"davisVisualization":{"isAvailable":true}}},"11":{"type":"markdown","content":"### Dashboard Variable Updates\n\n**with 1.313 in your DQL tiles now simply use one of the following:**\n\n*   $var => as before stays the default and will wrap your value in double quotation mark like \"value\" (unchanged)\n    \n*   $var **:noquote**   => value - e.g., for dql partials like duration (1m, 1d, ..)\n    \n*   $var **:backtick**  => \\`value \\` - e.g. for field names\n    \n*   $var **:triplequote**   => \"\"\"value\"\"\" e.g. for passing json\n\n\n\nDescriptions from the docs:\n\n1.  **Default Replacement**\n    \n    *   Example: $variable\n        \n    *   Description: Replaces the variable with its value using double quotes. Useful for Strings such as entity names or categories.\n        \n2.  **No Quote Replacement**:\n    \n    *   Example: $variable:noquote\n        \n    *   Description: Replaces the variable with its value without adding quotes. Useful for numbers, units, or function names. \n        \n3.  **Triple Quote Replacement**:\n    \n    *   Example: $variable:triplequote\n        \n    *   Description: Replaces the variable with its value using triple quotes. Useful for raw content such as JSON without escaping.\n        \n4.  **Backtick Replacement**:\n    \n    *   Example: $variable:backtick\n        \n    *   Description: Replaces the variable with its value using backticks. Useful for field or metric names.\n"}},"layouts":{"0":{"x":0,"y":15,"w":24,"h":4},"1":{"x":0,"y":11,"w":12,"h":4},"2":{"x":12,"y":11,"w":12,"h":4},"3":{"x":11,"y":22,"w":1